Port patch 4015 (ENHANCEMENT): SIXAXIS stick fallback. Killzone 2 turns valves and arms demolition charges by tilting
the pad; a pad with no motion sensor sends the rest values, so those sections cannot be finished. When the host pad
has no accelerometer and the game sees L1 and R1 both held, the X motion word follows the right stick:
X = 512 + 113 * tan(36 deg * s), s = right stick X in [-1, 1], with Y 399, Z 512, G 512 (a DS3 at rest; len 24 and
the PRESS_MODE capability were already reported). Full deflection is a 36 deg roll, inside the valve's +-35 deg hand
clamp and the charge's 33.4-37.3 deg arm windows. One shoulder alone sends the rest values, so the L1 zoom's
SIXAXIS aim correction (0x171698) is unchanged; pads with real sensors keep their own data. KZ2_MOTION_STICK=0 turns
it off. Game side (1.29): valve controller 0x127210 (grab buttons 0x127120), charge controller 0x119C90 (grab
buttons 0x119B88, read only while the charge's state +0x234 is 3), both EDeviceFunction 20/21 (GrabLeftHand,
GrabRightHand). The mapping is the pure header libs/input/pad_motion_stick.h; host test tools/runtime/test_motion_stick.sh.
The approach (an env-switchable stick stand-in for pads without motion) follows another ps3recomp port's description;
no code was taken from it.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

